police moving in on greenpeace  protesters in rotterdam campaigners with  the environmental pressure groups scaled  this silo belonging to shell as part of  a direct action they also blocked off  part of rotterdam port with this 30  meter boat while smaller vessels played  their parts calling for an end to all  fossil fuel advertising and sponsorship  in europe a new greenpeace report claims  two-thirds of recent social media ads by  the likes of shell and total amounted to  what it calls greenwashing it could  either be advertisement that show  renewable energy even if the renewable  energy constitutes only a very very tiny  percentage of their investments or it  could also be what we would call full  solutions so for instance a promoting  offsetting schemes that will allow you  know to continue driving your car as if  nothing has happened greenpeace is one  of more than 20 groups aiming to get a  million signatures for a petition to the  european commission if they do brussels  must consider passing legislation they  want a ban on advertising that includes  vehicles flights or ferries that run on  fossil fuels but here in the netherlands  it's the oil and gas firms under the  greatest pressure after a case brought  by environmental groups earlier this  year a court ordered royal dutch shell  to cut its global carbon emissions by  the end of 2030 by 45  of 2019 levels and the ruling warned of  an imminent violation of the company's  legal obligations to reduce dangers to  human life which it knew about  shell is appealing against that judgment  but activists hope things like the  petition will push it to act to curb the  growing climate emergency i'm confronted  with it daily i'm confronted with it  when i see the news when i see news  about refugees coming because there's no  possibility to live in their countries i  see it when the oil prices are rising in  england i see it in every day and i  think we should just act  shell says it respects the right to  protest